nel_summary\\\": \\\"This kernel is dense causal prefill attention (forward-only SDPA) with fixed B=16, Hq=8, Hkv=1, D=128 and variable sequence length S, computing O[b,h,i,:]=sum_{j<=i}softmax(scale*Q\\\\u00b7K)V using BF16 inputs/outputs and FP32 math in the reference. It is a mixed GEMM+reduction workload with quadratic S dependence, where dominant performance risks are repeated K/V traffic across causal steps and across 8 query heads sharing one KV head, plus occupancy pressure from FP32 online-softmax accumulators; best opportunities are streaming/online softmax (avoid SxS materialization), exploiting Hkv=1 cross-head K/V reuse, and adding a long-sequence decomposition path when S is large.\\\",\\n  \\\"open_questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"What seq_len distribution is expected in production (typical, p95, max), and is there a threshold where a separate long-S kernel is acceptable?\\\",\\n    \\\"Are q/k/v tensors guaranteed contiguous in the last dimension and what are exact runtime strides/alignment guarantees for BF16 vectorized access?\\\",\\n    \\\"What numerical tolerance is required versus PyTorch SDPA (max abs/rel error), and is deterministic reproducibility required across runs/devices?\\\",\\n    \\\"Should sm_scale be treated as compile-time-constant-like across calls or fully dynamic, and can we assume finite/non-NaN inputs only?\\\",\\n    \\\"Is there an existing baseline HIP kernel latency for MI300X to anchor speedup targets, and what stream/concurrency context will this kernel run under?\\\",\\n    \\\"Can we allocate temporary workspace for split-sequence merge paths, or must the kernel be strictly workspace-free?\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n[KSEARCH HIP HARD CONSTRAINTS]\\n- main.cpp MUST NOT contain kernel launch syntax `<<< >>>`.\\n- main.cpp MUST NOT call `hipLaunchKernelGGL`.\\n- main.cpp must call host launch wrappers declared in kernel.h with this pattern:\\n  `hipError_t ksearch_launch_<kernel>(dim3 grid, dim3 block, size_t shared_mem, hipStream_t s