"{\"input\":\"You are improving a HIP C++ kernel on MI300X.\\nThe current implementation may be correct-but-slower-than-desired, or it may have regressed.\\n\\nOriginal Specification:\\nName: dense_qkv_prefill_causal_h8_kv1_d128_bs16\\nType: dense_attention\\n\\nAxes:\\n  batch_size: constant = 16\\n  num_q_heads: constant = 8\\n  num_kv_heads: constant = 1\\n  seq_len: variable (Sequence length for prefill. q/k/v share the same sequence length.)\\n  head_dim: constant = 128\\n\\nInputs:\\n  q: [batch_size, num_q_heads, seq_len, head_dim] (DType.BFLOAT16)\\n  k: [batch_size, num_kv_heads, seq_len, head_dim] (DType.BFLOAT16)\\n  v: [batch_size, num_kv_heads, seq_len, head_dim] (DType.BFLOAT16)\\n  sm_scale: scalar (DType.FLOAT32) - Softmax scale, usually 1/sqrt(head_dim).\\n\\nOutputs:\\n  output: [batch_size, num_q_heads, seq_len, head_dim] (DType.BFLOAT16) - Dense causal prefill attention output.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n  - batch_size == 16\\n  - head_dim == 128\\n  - num_kv_heads == 1\\n  - num_q_heads == 8\\n\\n\\nReference Implementation:\\nimport torch\\n\\n\\n@torch.no_grad()\\ndef run(q, k, v, sm_scale):\\n    # dense SDPA reference (forward-only, causal prefill)\\n    assert q.ndim == 4 and k.ndim == 4 and v.ndim == 4\\n    bq, hq, sq, dq = q.shape\\n    bk, hk, sk, dk = k.shape\\n    bv, hv, sv, dv = v.shape\\n\\n    assert (bq, sq, dq) == (bk, sk, dk) == (bv, sv, dv)\\n    assert hq == 8\\n    assert bq == 16\\n    assert hk == 1\\n    assert hv == hk\\n    assert dq == 128\\n\\n    if hk == 1:\\n        k = k.repeat_interleave(8, dim=1)\\n        v = v.repeat_interleave(8, dim=1)\\n\\n    q = q.to(torch.float32)\\n    k = k.to(torch.float32)\\n    v = v.to(torch.float32)\\n\\n    out = torch.nn.functional.scaled_dot_product_attention(\\n        q,\\n        k,\\n        v,\\n        attn_mask=None,\\n        dropout_p=0.0,\\n        is_causal=True,\\n        scale=float(sm_scale),\\n    )\\n    return out.to(torch.bfloat16)\\n\\nCycle-Best Base Implementation