"This is a dense causal prefill attention forward kernel (GQA/MQA-style with hq=8, hk=1, d=128, b=16) that computes O=softmax(scale\\\\u00b7QK^T_causal)V with BF16 inputs and BF16 output, typically using FP32 internal math; it is a matrix-multiply-like workload with row-wise reductions and strong K/V reuse opportunity across 8 query heads because KV head count is 1. Main performance risks are regime-dependent: launch/sync overhead at small seq_len, mixed compute+memory limits at medium seq_len, and HBM traffic plus register-pressure/occupancy collapse at large seq_len, especially when storing FP32 accumulators for online softmax over long causal prefixes.\\\",\\n  \\\"open_questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"What seq_len distribution is expected in production (e.g., typical, P95, max), and do we need separate tuned paths by regime?\\\",\\n    \\\"Are q/k/v contiguous in the last dimension and what are exact runtime strides/alignment guarantees for vector-friendly loads?\\\",\\n    \\\"What numerical tolerance is required versus PyTorch SDPA (ULP/relative error), and is full FP32 accumulation mandatory for logits and V accumulation?\\\",\\n    \\\"Is temporary workspace allowed (and how much) for multi-stage or split-reduction variants?\\\",\\n    \\\"Are q, k, v guaranteed to be non-overlapping buffers and resident in HBM (not unified/pageable) during launch?\\\",\\n    \\\"Should sm_scale be treated as arbitrary runtime scalar or fixed to 1/sqrt(128), enabling compile-time specialization?\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n[KSEARCH HIP HARD CONSTRAINTS]\\n- main.cpp MUST NOT contain kernel launch syntax `<<< >>>`.\\n- main.cpp MUST NOT call `hipLaunchKernelGGL`.\\n- main.cpp must call host launch wrappers declared in kernel.h with this pattern:\\n  `hipError_t ksearch_launch_<kernel>(dim3 grid, dim3 block, size_t shared_mem, hipStream_t stream, ...);`\\n- kernel.cu must implement those wrappers and perform actual `<<< >>>` launches there.\\n- Do NOT include private HIP headers under `hip/a